Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.43,0:03:00.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Good morning, Quark.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.52,0:03:05.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Couldn't believe it.\NLisa told Janet
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.64,0:03:08.31,Default,,0,0,0,,that Paul asked Barbara to ask me\Nif I had a date to the dance.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.23,0:03:11.86,Default,,0,0,0,,No. They broke up\Nfor religious differences.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.94,0:03:14.07,Default,,0,0,0,,She thought she was God\Nand he disagreed.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.41,0:03:18.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, this afternoon\Naround five.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.16,0:03:20.91,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm meeting him at the mall.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.99,0:03:23.62,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't know. Maybe. Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.66,0:03:26.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, I can't.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.71,0:03:29.00,Default,,0,0,0,,I've got to hang around awhile\Nand keep an eye on Nick.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.54,0:03:31.13,Default,,0,0,0,,He likes to take things apart.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.63,0:03:34.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, that's why I watch it\Nat your house.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.67,0:03:37.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Things will cool off after today.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.97,0:03:39.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Dad has his big "show and tell"\Nat the lab.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:41.39,0:03:42.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Zap!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:43.89,0:03:47.56,Default,,0,0,0,,- It works! It really works!\N- Nick, get real.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.85,0:03:50.94,Default,,0,0,0,,The subject... has disappeared.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.06,0:03:52.73,Default,,0,0,0,,No, no, it's not that.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.53,0:03:54.78,Default,,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:55.53,0:03:57.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Mom and Dad\Nhad an argument last night,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.66,0:03:59.28,Default,,0,0,0,,and Mom spent the night at Grandma's.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.70,0:04:01.32,Default,,0,0,0,,I think she needed a rest.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.66,0:04:03.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Right.\NHer and me both.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.79,0:04:04.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.66,0:04:07.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay. Bye.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.67,0:04:15.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Amy... when's Mom coming home?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.30,0:04:19.30,Default,,0,0,0,,She's working, Nick.\NShe'll be home this afternoon.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.64,0:04:24.22,Default,,0,0,0,,If only Dad could get\Nthat machine to work.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.62,0:04:48.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Breakfast.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.00,0:04:52.67,Default,,0,0,0,,I need a couple of minutes here.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.92,0:05:00.30,Default,,0,0,0,,"I'll be down in five minutes."
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.93,0:05:03.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Typing with his gloves on again.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.62,0:05:35.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, no, not again!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.54,0:05:37.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Who does he think he is,\NMister Wizard?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.80,0:05:43.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Szalinski, give it a rest!\NIt's Saturday!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.68,0:05:47.31,Default,,0,0,0,,It's construction, honey.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.39,0:05:49.48,Default,,0,0,0,,You of all people\Nshould understand that.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.64,0:05:50.06,Default,,0,0,0,,- You're much bigger than he is.\N- Szalinski!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.98,0:05:53.56,Default,,0,0,0,,- Honey, can't we--\N- Hold it, Dad.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.65,0:05:55.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't move.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.52,0:05:57.94,Default,,0,0,0,,- Ron, what are you doing?\N- Defending the backyard, Dad.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.07,0:05:59.28,Default,,0,0,0,,That's my fishing rod!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.36,0:06:00.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Dad, no!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.32,0:06:02.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Dad!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.32,0:06:06.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Am I bleeding?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.41,0:06:08.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Honey, it's rubber.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.29,0:06:11.04,Default,,0,0,0,,- Dad, I told you not to move.\N- What's on this thing?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.66,0:06:14.04,Default,,0,0,0,,- Super Glue.\N- Super Glue?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.29,0:06:15.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Gotta mark those trespassers, Dad.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.08,0:06:17.59,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm not a trespasser.\NI'm your father!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.67,0:06:19.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Better wash it off quick, hon.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.38,0:06:21.55,Default,,0,0,0,,- It's taking the skin off.\N- I'll talk to you later.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.71,0:06:24.13,Default,,0,0,0,,- What's with this kid?\N- He's 12.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.30,0:06:25.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Attila the Hun\Nwas 12 once, too, you know.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.05,0:06:27.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, come on!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.10,0:06:30.31,Default,,0,0,0,,He's sounding.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.77,0:06:35.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Weird family.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.08,0:06:51.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Dad?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.95,0:06:53.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Look, I finished mine.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.100,0:06:56.33,Default,,0,0,0,,- Looks just like yours, huh?\N- That's great, Nick.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.46,0:06:59.34,Default,,0,0,0,,You know, Dad, I was calculating.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.59,0:07:00.71,Default,,0,0,0,,If you took all the molecules\Nin this house--
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.80,0:07:03.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Listen, Nick, I gotta get this thing\Nworking before I leave.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.17,0:07:04.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Why don't you help your sister?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.18,0:07:49.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Stay back, boy.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.76,0:07:50.76,Default,,0,0,0,,If this thing works,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.85,0:07:53.43,Default,,0,0,0,,this'll put us right up there\Nwith the invention of electricity,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.64,0:07:56.31,Default,,0,0,0,,the first man in space.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.39,0:07:57.64,Default,,0,0,0,,First dog in space.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.65,0:08:08.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on! Shrink!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:08.90,0:08:09.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Shrink!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.29,0:08:20.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Please, please, shrink.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.79,0:08:21.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Shrink!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.64,0:08:37.43,Default,,0,0,0,,On the other hand,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.52,0:08:40.14,Default,,0,0,0,,we've come up with an interesting way\Nof making applesauce.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.48,0:08:46.61,Default,,0,0,0,,You got it, honey.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.69,0:08:48.24,Default,,0,0,0,,- Sure?\N- Positive.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:48.36,0:08:51.41,Default,,0,0,0,,You're wiping away brain cells,\Nand there aren't many to spare.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.53,0:08:54.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Everybody in my family's a comedian.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:54.62,0:08:56.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Everybody except you, hon.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:57.62,0:08:58.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Darn right.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:01.50,0:09:03.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, look who's decided\Nto join the land of the living.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.75,0:09:06.71,Default,,0,0,0,,And is Russell ready\Nfor his big fishing trip?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.55,0:09:08.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Not really, Dad.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.38,0:09:10.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Not really?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.55,0:09:12.51,Default,,0,0,0,,There's a big fish out there\Nwith your name on it.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.76,0:09:15.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Fishing's your thing,\NDad, not mine.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.89,0:09:20.85,Default,,0,0,0,,- What's the matter with him?\N- Shh!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.94,0:09:22.10,Default,,0,0,0,,What do you mean "shush"?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.23,0:09:24.94,Default,,0,0,0,,I see nothing wrong\Nwith wanting to take my son fishing.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.86,0:09:27.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Russel, I shouldn't\Nbe telling you this,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:27.61,0:09:29.49,Default,,0,0,0,,but he was cut\Nfrom the football team yesterday.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:29.57,0:09:30.99,Default,,0,0,0,,- What?\N- Honey, please!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.07,0:09:32.86,Default,,0,0,0,,What he doesn't need right now\Nis to hear from you.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:32.95,0:09:33.87,Default,,0,0,0,,He needs something.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.95,0:09:35.78,Default,,0,0,0,,- When I was his age, I was cap--\N- Captain of the team.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.87,0:09:37.66,Default,,0,0,0,,And if my father wanted me\Nto go on a fishing trip,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.74,0:09:38.87,Default,,0,0,0,,- I would've been--\N- Been grateful.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.95,0:09:40.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Russ, he is too small for football.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:41.04,0:09:43.42,Default,,0,0,0,,- He is not too small for football!\N- Too small!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.50,0:09:45.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Shh! Honey, when you say\Nthings like that,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.79,0:09:47.04,Default,,0,0,0,,you make him feel about this big.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.13,0:09:50.05,Default,,0,0,0,,If he wants to feel big,\Nhe should act big.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.30,0:09:56.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Elbows up.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.56,0:10:01.77,Default,,0,0,0,,What's the matter with you?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.85,0:10:03.06,Default,,0,0,0,,I am on a special diet.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:03.52,0:10:05.31,Default,,0,0,0,,- No toxic waste.\N- Fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.94,0:10:09.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Here, Quark.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:13.57,0:10:15.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Eat it, Dad, before it gets cold.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.50,0:10:23.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Mmm, did you get the machine to work?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.33,0:10:25.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:25.58,0:10:27.17,Default,,0,0,0,,A few more bugs to get out, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:27.96,0:10:29.13,Default,,0,0,0,,What about the conference?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:31.92,0:10:33.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Jeez, the conference.\NI gotta get going.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.22,0:10:37.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Dad! Dad, wait.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.89,0:10:38.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Dad!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:39.05,0:10:41.35,Default,,0,0,0,,If Mom calls, tell her\NI'll be home by lunchtime.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.43,0:10:43.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Dad, don't forget my dress\Nfrom the cleaners,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:43.35,0:10:45.69,Default,,0,0,0,,- Nick's allergy pills--\N- It's all in my head. Don't worry.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.15,0:10:47.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Wish me luck!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:47.77,0:10:49.36,Default,,0,0,0,,I need luck getting out\Nof this door.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.07,0:10:57.37,Default,,0,0,0,,House of Insanity.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:58.16,0:10:59.91,Default,,0,0,0,,- Hi, honey.\N<i>- Hi, Mom.</i>
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.16,0:11:01.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Nick, go get Dad.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.33,0:11:03.25,Default,,0,0,0,,He's just leaving for the conference.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:03.33,0:11:05.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Dad, it's Mom.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.54,0:11:07.88,Default,,0,0,0,,- Where?\N- On the phone!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.50,0:11:09.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.34,0:11:10.75,Default,,0,0,0,,How did everything go this morning?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:10.88,0:11:12.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Boy, did we miss you.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.01,0:11:14.34,Default,,0,0,0,,I missed you too, honey.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:14.80,0:11:16.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Did Paul Tate ask you to the dance?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:16.38,0:11:17.93,Default,,0,0,0,,I think he's going to.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:18.01,0:11:19.72,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm gonna meet him\Nat the mall later today.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:20.10,0:11:21.51,Default,,0,0,0,,- Here's Dad.\N- Thanks.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:22.22,0:11:23.43,Default,,0,0,0,,- Hiya.\N<i>- Hi.</i>
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.52,0:11:24.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Nick!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.43,0:11:26.02,Default,,0,0,0,,I called to wish you\Nthe luck at the conference.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.27,0:11:27.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Look, Diane,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.77,0:11:28.90,Default,,0,0,0,,if things go well this morning,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.98,0:11:30.90,Default,,0,0,0,,everything will change around here,\NI promise you.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.15,0:11:33.40,Default,,0,0,0,,<i>Okay. I have a house to show,</i>
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.11,0:11:36.20,Default,,0,0,0,,and then I'll be home this afternoon\Nand we'll talk.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:36.28,0:11:37.28,Default,,0,0,0,,<i>Good luck today.</i>
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.40,0:11:39.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Thanks. Bye, honey.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.49,0:11:42.53,Default,,0,0,0,,- What time is Mom coming home?\N- Later.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:42.79,0:11:44.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Listen, we got to make this place\Nspick and span. Okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.70,0:11:47.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Nick, I want you to mow the lawn.\NAmy...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.75,0:11:51.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Good luck.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:03.10,0:12:06.35,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm helping my dad with this\Nreal important new invention.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:06.68,0:12:08.48,Default,,0,0,0,,So, um...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.56,0:12:11.61,Default,,0,0,0,,I... I'll let you mow half my yard.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.52,0:12:13.90,Default,,0,0,0,,No, thanks.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.24,0:12:18.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Wow! With that?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.36,0:12:19.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.20,0:12:22.62,Default,,0,0,0,,And... this.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:25.91,0:12:27.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, it's a remote control!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:28.66,0:12:31.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Tell you what.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.58,0:12:35.38,Default,,0,0,0,,You throw in... a box of cookies,\NI'll let you cut the whole thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:36.59,0:12:39.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, but I have to go\Nand meet Newt right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.64,0:12:43.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Uh, could I do it later?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.05,0:12:45.31,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't think so,\Nbecause, you know,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:45.39,0:12:47.18,Default,,0,0,0,,- my dad's gonna come home and...\N- Aw, come on!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.81,0:12:50.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay. Don't be too late.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.69,0:12:51.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay, thanks.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.27,0:12:53.57,Default,,0,0,0,,No problem.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.86,0:12:55.11,Default,,0,0,0,,See you later!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.11,0:13:03.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Nothing like a hard day's work.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.16,0:13:09.58,Default,,0,0,0,,French fries,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.62,0:13:12.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Tater sticks,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.63,0:13:15.79,Default,,0,0,0,,meat loaf,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.00,0:13:18.88,Default,,0,0,0,,veal "parmedjian."
Dialogue: 0,0:13:19.22,0:13:20.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, Dad.\NWanna go play some baseball?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.43,0:13:23.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Hmm, baseball...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:24.55,0:13:25.60,Default,,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.97,0:13:27.72,Default,,0,0,0,,I gotta load the camper, Ron.\NI'm busy.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.85,0:13:30.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, Russ, pitch for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:48.41,0:13:49.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, Szalinski,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.37,0:13:52.25,Default,,0,0,0,,ever do anything normal,\Nlike play baseball?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:52.46,0:13:53.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Nope.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:54.79,0:13:56.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Baseball's for mortals.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.63,0:13:58.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe you could be the base.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:59.38,0:14:00.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe you could be the mound.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.30,0:14:02.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Ronald!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:02.88,0:14:04.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Lug your stuff.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:04.84,0:14:06.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Later, worm.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:13.52,0:14:15.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Russell, give me a hand here.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:18.69,0:14:21.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Russell! Give me a hand here.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.11,0:14:25.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Dad, it's early.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:26.20,0:14:28.87,Default,,0,0,0,,The early worm catches the fish,\NRussell.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.45,0:14:31.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Remember that.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.29,0:14:35.92,Default,,0,0,0,,The Forresters are coming by\Nafter lunch, so come on! Quick march!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.95,0:15:11.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Weird family.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.56,0:15:33.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Russell...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:35.85,0:15:39.23,Default,,0,0,0,,I know it seems strange\Nwhen you look at me today, but,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:39.65,0:15:40.86,Default,,0,0,0,,when I was your age,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:41.15,0:15:43.07,Default,,0,0,0,,I was not much bigger than you.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.86,0:15:45.82,Default,,0,0,0,,I know, Dad. You've told me\Nabout a million times.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.90,0:15:47.45,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, just hear me out.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.65,0:15:50.49,Default,,0,0,0,,The point is,\Ncoach put me on these babies.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.99,0:15:52.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Know what happened?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.78,0:15:55.54,Default,,0,0,0,,I put on 20 pounds\Nof pure, unadulterated,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:55.62,0:15:57.87,Default,,0,0,0,,blitz-the-quarterback and\Nrip-his-head-off muscle, Russell.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.83,0:16:00.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, I'll make you a little bet.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:01.25,0:16:04.09,Default,,0,0,0,,If you work out for... three months,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.38,0:16:07.59,Default,,0,0,0,,you will be throwing farther,\Nyou will be running faster,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:07.76,0:16:10.72,Default,,0,0,0,,and you will be hitting harder\Nthan anybody else on that team.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.50,0:16:36.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Go ahead, go ahead.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.83,0:16:42.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Um, Dad, you know\Nthe weights aren't my thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.09,0:16:45.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Fishing isn't your thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.21,0:16:49.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Weights aren't your thing.\NJust what is your thing?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:52.18,0:16:53.43,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't know,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.80,0:16:55.51,Default,,0,0,0,,but I'll keep you posted, okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.14,0:16:59.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Fine, until you do,\Nyou're trying these,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:59.94,0:17:02.61,Default,,0,0,0,,and you're coming fishing\Nwith the family. Is that clear?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.86,0:17:05.90,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't hear you!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.78,0:17:08.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.24,0:17:10.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Better.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.70,0:17:12.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Uh...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:13.53,0:17:15.49,Default,,0,0,0,,lift with your legs,\Nnot with your back.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.05,0:17:31.88,Default,,0,0,0,,What am I doing wrong, Spike?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.43,0:17:42.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Russell, you're not smoking\Na cigarette, are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.89,0:17:44.98,Default,,0,0,0,,No, dear.\NYou know I've given that up.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:59.16,0:18:01.25,Default,,0,0,0,,- Your stuff all loaded?\N- Ready to fire.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:01.66,0:18:03.50,Default,,0,0,0,,We've got the best spot on the lake.\NYou looking forward to it?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.58,0:18:04.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Tubular!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:06.42,0:18:08.96,Default,,0,0,0,,He's only 12 and he's\Nalready thinking about construction.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.30,0:18:12.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Why can't Russell be more like that?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.09,0:18:14.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, honey, just give him a chance.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:22.18,0:18:23.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Ron Thompson at the plate.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.69,0:18:25.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Bottom of the 9th. Clutch situation.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:26.02,0:18:27.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Here comes the pitch!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:27.90,0:18:30.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, he's swinging like a rusty gate!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.49,0:18:33.61,Default,,0,0,0,,He pumps once, pumps twice. Oh!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.03,0:18:36.49,Default,,0,0,0,,He's never been good\Non the high outside pitch.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.78,0:18:39.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Here it comes.\NThe fastball is bread and butter.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.91,0:18:40.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Grand...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.100,0:18:45.04,Default,,0,0,0,,slam.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.46,0:18:51.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, hey, I didn't do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.51,0:18:53.01,Default,,0,0,0,,- Come on, dope.\N- Nobody has to know.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.09,0:18:54.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Nobody saw it but you!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:55.01,0:18:58.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's negotiate.\NI'm your brother, Russ.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:58.30,0:19:00.14,Default,,0,0,0,,You're not supposed\Nto fink on your own bother!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:01.64,0:19:04.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Turn me in, and I'll tell all what\Nyou spend your allowance on!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.48,0:19:05.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, Russ.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:07.73,0:19:10.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Look, either you tell 'em,\Nor I tell 'em, okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:12.19,0:19:14.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay, you tell 'em.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.75,0:19:32.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Aren't you in the wrong yard?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.46,0:19:34.01,Default,,0,0,0,,- Listen, nerd face...\N- Tell 'em!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.38,0:19:35.47,Default,,0,0,0,,What's going on?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.01,0:19:37.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Hi. Um...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:38.89,0:19:40.85,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm Russ Thompson from next door.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:41.89,0:19:42.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Um...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:43.56,0:19:45.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Um, my brother has\Nsomething to tell you.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:45.85,0:19:47.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Or else I can tell her.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:47.19,0:19:48.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:48.73,0:19:50.36,Default,,0,0,0,,See, I was playing\Nwith my ball, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:50.48,0:19:53.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, actually, it's not my ball\Nexactly. It's Charlie Sudzen's...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:53.57,0:19:54.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Just tell her what you did.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:54.78,0:19:57.24,Default,,0,0,0,,It never would have happened\Nif their house wasn't so close.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:58.11,0:19:59.78,Default,,0,0,0,,He hit a baseball\Nthrough your attic window.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:59.91,0:20:00.83,Default,,0,0,0,,He what?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:00.91,0:20:03.91,Default,,0,0,0,,It shouldn't have been closed\Nin the first place. It's a nice day!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:03.99,0:20:06.04,Default,,0,0,0,,We'll get it fixed, okay? We'll take\Nit out of his allowance, all right?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:06.12,0:20:07.75,Default,,0,0,0,,My allowance? Dream on.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:07.83,0:20:09.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay. We'll just have\NDad pay for it, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.50,0:20:12.75,Default,,0,0,0,,We'll take it out of my allowance.\NGive me my ball back.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:12.84,0:20:15.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Until you pay, no man shall pass.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:15.71,0:20:17.67,Default,,0,0,0,,You've got nothing to say about it,\Nspace boy.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:17.76,0:20:18.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Cool it!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:20.14,0:20:22.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Nick, take him upstairs\Nand get him his ball.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:22.51,0:20:23.97,Default,,0,0,0,,- And clean up the mess.\N- What?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:24.06,0:20:26.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Do it, Nick.\NI don't have time to mess around.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:28.60,0:20:29.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:29.56,0:20:32.40,Default,,0,0,0,,This is what's wrong\Nwith the American system of justice.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.94,0:20:34.98,Default,,0,0,0,,So...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.57,0:20:37.94,Default,,0,0,0,,You like to dance, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:39.28,0:20:40.49,Default,,0,0,0,,How do you know?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:42.28,0:20:43.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Well...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:43.12,0:20:44.83,Default,,0,0,0,,- You could see me?\N- No!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:44.91,0:20:46.62,Default,,0,0,0,,No... Yeah, I could...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:47.62,0:20:49.04,Default,,0,0,0,,but I wasn't watching you, I...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:53.00,0:20:54.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Awesome.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:54.75,0:20:57.26,Default,,0,0,0,,So your dad's still in contact\Nwith his home planet.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:09.10,0:21:11.90,Default,,0,0,0,,And given that my machine\Ncan substantially reduce the size
Dialogue: 0,0:21:11.98,0:21:13.98,Default,,0,0,0,,of bulky payloads...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:15.36,0:21:16.86,Default,,0,0,0,,and fuel supplies,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:17.15,0:21:19.61,Default,,0,0,0,,the savings to the space program\Nwould be staggering.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:19.90,0:21:21.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Mr. Szalinski,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:21.40,0:21:24.37,Default,,0,0,0,,are you trying to tell me that\Nsuddenly size is no longer relative?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:24.66,0:21:26.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, that's right,\NProfessor Fredrickson,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:26.49,0:21:29.37,Default,,0,0,0,,that all matter is made up of not\Nonly density, but of empty space.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:29.45,0:21:31.08,Default,,0,0,0,,And if we can proportionately reduce
Dialogue: 0,0:21:31.16,0:21:32.88,Default,,0,0,0,,the amount of empty space\Nin any given object,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.96,0:21:34.84,Default,,0,0,0,,we can thereby... shrink the object.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.92,0:21:36.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Uh-huh. Where's your proof?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:37.88,0:21:40.01,Default,,0,0,0,,When Einstein came up\Nwith the atomic bomb,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:40.13,0:21:41.68,Default,,0,0,0,,did they ask him to prove\Nthat it worked?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:42.18,0:21:44.89,Default,,0,0,0,,You, Mr. Szalinski,\Nare hardly Einstein.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:47.22,0:21:48.35,Default,,0,0,0,,I picked a name.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:48.47,0:21:50.64,Default,,0,0,0,,You have, however, managed\Nto shrink one thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:50.98,0:21:52.69,Default,,0,0,0,,The size of this audience.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:52.98,0:21:55.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Gentlemen, ladies,\NI don't know about you,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:55.11,0:21:56.57,Default,,0,0,0,,but I'm going to lunch.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:04.49,0:22:06.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Wayne? Wayne!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:07.28,0:22:10.37,Default,,0,0,0,,- Oh, hi, Dr. Brainard.\N- Don't take it too hard, Wayne.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:10.66,0:22:13.33,Default,,0,0,0,,It will take time\Nto convince people without proof.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:14.12,0:22:16.00,Default,,0,0,0,,I appreciate it.\NThanks a lot.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:17.80,0:22:20.71,Default,,0,0,0,,By the way, you were right\Nabout the electric flea collar.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:20.80,0:22:22.63,Default,,0,0,0,,The extension cord was a bad idea.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:23.59,0:22:25.26,Default,,0,0,0,,What could be taking them so long?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:26.89,0:22:28.85,Default,,0,0,0,,I am not missing the mall today.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:30.02,0:22:31.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Nick!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:34.56,0:22:35.81,Default,,0,0,0,,- Nick.\N- Ron?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:35.90,0:22:38.07,Default,,0,0,0,,If you guys are hiding up here,\Nit's not funny.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:39.15,0:22:40.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Nick, you know what Dad said.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:41.28,0:22:43.19,Default,,0,0,0,,You're not supposed\Nto be playing up here.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:58.79,0:23:00.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Where are we?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:13.02,0:23:14.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, my God. What happened?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:14.43,0:23:16.02,Default,,0,0,0,,- Amy!\N- Russ!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:16.56,0:23:18.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Amy!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:19.65,0:23:20.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Nicky.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:20.73,0:23:21.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Ron?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:24.94,0:23:26.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Nick, what happened?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:26.40,0:23:28.03,Default,,0,0,0,,We're all the size of boogers!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:31.83,0:23:33.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Be quiet, Quark!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:36.12,0:23:37.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Nick, what did you do?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:37.42,0:23:39.92,Default,,0,0,0,,- Me? It was his ball.\N- Shut up, wimp!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:39.92,0:23:40.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Can somebody get that?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:40.21,0:23:42.34,Default,,0,0,0,,- What's that?\N- It's Dad's thinking couch.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:48.68,0:23:50.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Amy? Nick?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:50.76,0:23:51.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Hello?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:56.48,0:23:57.69,Default,,0,0,0,,It's not for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:00.69,0:24:02.11,Default,,0,0,0,,What is it, Quark?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:02.19,0:24:04.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Nick!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:05.90,0:24:07.95,Default,,0,0,0,,- Listen.\N- Are you guys home?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:08.24,0:24:10.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Sounds like Dad. He'll fix us.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:10.41,0:24:12.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Mr. Szalinski, up here!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:13.20,0:24:14.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Up here, Dad!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:14.79,0:24:16.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Quick, over there by the door,\Nokay? Get that side!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:17.16,0:24:18.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Is anybody up there?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:18.41,0:24:20.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Nick, get off and give us a hand!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:22.46,0:24:24.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Nick? Amy?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:24.76,0:24:26.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, Amy, your date's here.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:27.30,0:24:28.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, gross.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:29.01,0:24:30.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Watch out for the crack!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:36.10,0:24:37.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Hurry up. He's coming!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:51.91,0:24:54.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Right here, Mr. Szalinski.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:56.29,0:24:57.70,Default,,0,0,0,,- Dad!\N- Dad!
Dialogue: 0,0:25:06.88,0:25:09.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Help, help!
Dialogue: 0,0:25:17.43,0:25:18.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Where's my couch?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:24.52,0:25:27.40,Default,,0,0,0,,- What is he, deaf?\N- Don't you get it?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:27.86,0:25:29.94,Default,,0,0,0,,We're too small. He can't hear us.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:35.28,0:25:36.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Dad!
Dialogue: 0,0:25:41.12,0:25:43.42,Default,,0,0,0,,- Move over!\N- Ow! Watch out!
Dialogue: 0,0:25:57.97,0:25:59.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, my God.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:01.98,0:26:04.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Reminds me of the backyard.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:06.06,0:26:08.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Something tells me\Nwe're not going fishing this weekend.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:08.57,0:26:10.36,Default,,0,0,0,,That should make you happy.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:10.44,0:26:12.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Blow it\Nout your shorts, Ron.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:12.32,0:26:13.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Dad can fix us, right Nick?
Dialogue: 0,0:26:14.45,0:26:17.03,Default,,0,0,0,,I... I think so.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:17.58,0:26:19.04,Default,,0,0,0,,RON; Oh, great.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:19.58,0:26:20.95,Default,,0,0,0,,We just have to get back\Nto the house.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:21.04,0:26:22.100,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm never going back to your house!
Dialogue: 0,0:26:23.62,0:26:24.83,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm going home.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:25.92,0:26:27.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, Russ.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:30.96,0:26:33.22,Default,,0,0,0,,- Russ?\N- Tell me the truth.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:33.92,0:26:35.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Can your dad help us?
Dialogue: 0,0:26:35.26,0:26:37.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Russ, we're supposed\Nto go fishing.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:37.76,0:26:39.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, right. How're you going,\Nas bait?
Dialogue: 0,0:26:41.68,0:26:42.98,Default,,0,0,0,,What a witch!
Dialogue: 0,0:26:56.16,0:26:58.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Russ, you coming down or what?
Dialogue: 0,0:26:59.08,0:27:00.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, we can't stay here.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:02.100,0:27:04.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, I think we should\Nstick together.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:07.08,0:27:08.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, come on.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:14.34,0:27:15.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Nicky!
Dialogue: 0,0:27:37.20,0:27:39.37,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't think we're\Nin Kansas anymore, Toto.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:40.66,0:27:43.12,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't think we're\Nin the food chain anymore, Dorothy.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:50.13,0:27:51.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, Ron.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:51.09,0:27:52.75,Default,,0,0,0,,- We're gonna go with them.\N- What?
Dialogue: 0,0:27:53.59,0:27:55.80,Default,,0,0,0,,You let a girl tell\Nyou what to do? Mmm.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:56.84,0:27:59.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Look, Ron. Down here,\Nyou're gonna listen to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:59.39,0:28:01.51,Default,,0,0,0,,From now on, you're gonna do\Nwhat I say!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:02.39,0:28:03.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Run!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:20.41,0:28:23.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Great Sir Russell Thompson,\Nstalking the rogue butterfly.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:23.62,0:28:24.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Knock it off, Ron.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:26.25,0:28:29.50,Default,,0,0,0,,We're now a quarter\Nof an inch tall, and...
Dialogue: 0,0:28:30.04,0:28:32.00,Default,,0,0,0,,64 feet from the house.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:32.63,0:28:35.51,Default,,0,0,0,,That's the equivalent of 3.2 miles.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:36.09,0:28:39.01,Default,,0,0,0,,That's a long way,\Neven for a man of science.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:39.17,0:28:41.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Nick, I've got six hours\Nto get home,
Dialogue: 0,0:28:41.59,0:28:43.31,Default,,0,0,0,,get big, and get to the mall.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:44.22,0:28:45.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Now get moving!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:48.18,0:28:52.36,Default,,0,0,0,,That butterfly\Nhad a wingspan of 42 feet!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:52.56,0:28:53.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Nick!
Dialogue: 0,0:29:08.62,0:29:09.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Hi.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:10.46,0:29:11.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Hi.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:13.08,0:29:14.29,Default,,0,0,0,,- Look, Diane...\N- Guess what I saw...
Dialogue: 0,0:29:15.80,0:29:17.84,Default,,0,0,0,,- I sold a house.\N- Really? That's great!
Dialogue: 0,0:29:17.92,0:29:21.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, you know that big estate?\NThe Boorsteins bought it.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:21.13,0:29:23.39,Default,,0,0,0,,I only had to show it\Nto them 12 times.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:23.89,0:29:25.31,Default,,0,0,0,,How'd your conference go?
Dialogue: 0,0:29:26.06,0:29:27.43,Default,,0,0,0,,I got a lot of laughs.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:27.93,0:29:30.60,Default,,0,0,0,,- Oh, Wayne.\N- I failed, Diane. I'm...
Dialogue: 0,0:29:31.19,0:29:34.36,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm just gonna get my old job back,\Nif I can get my old job back.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:34.61,0:29:36.98,Default,,0,0,0,,But from now on,\Nthings are gonna be different.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:37.28,0:29:38.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Different.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:40.11,0:29:41.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:44.45,0:29:45.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Where are the kids?
Dialogue: 0,0:29:45.87,0:29:48.12,Default,,0,0,0,,I haven't seen them\Nsince I left this morning.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:48.54,0:29:49.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Did you tell them\NI was coming home?
Dialogue: 0,0:29:49.95,0:29:51.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, that's why\Nthey cleaned things up.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:52.46,0:29:53.75,Default,,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:54.29,0:29:55.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, they're probably\Njust at the mall.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:59.01,0:30:01.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Want to hear something strange?\NMy thinking couch is missing.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:02.72,0:30:05.26,Default,,0,0,0,,- The one from the attic?\N- Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:14.02,0:30:17.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, Ron. This is a lot better than\Nthose nature hikes Dad drags...
Dialogue: 0,0:30:19.36,0:30:22.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Nick, don't you ever\Npick up your toys?
Dialogue: 0,0:30:22.90,0:30:24.11,Default,,0,0,0,,What a wimp!
Dialogue: 0,0:30:24.66,0:30:26.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Been looking for that guy.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:30.33,0:30:31.83,Default,,0,0,0,,It's already one o'clock.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:32.45,0:30:33.66,Default,,0,0,0,,So much for the mall.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:34.04,0:30:35.67,Default,,0,0,0,,What if time shrunk, too?\NI mean,
Dialogue: 0,0:30:35.75,0:30:39.34,Default,,0,0,0,,what if it's hours to us, but it's\Nyears to the rest of the world?
Dialogue: 0,0:30:39.75,0:30:42.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay, that would be cool.\NAll my teachers would be retired.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:42.46,0:30:45.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Impossible. Time doesn't exist,\Nexcept as a...
Dialogue: 0,0:30:45.26,0:30:46.51,Default,,0,0,0,,No...
Dialogue: 0,0:30:46.85,0:30:48.56,Default,,0,0,0,,What's a river doing\Nin your yard?
Dialogue: 0,0:30:48.85,0:30:50.35,Default,,0,0,0,,It's not a river, dope.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:50.43,0:30:52.98,Default,,0,0,0,,It could be a stream of dog pee\Nand it looks like a river to us.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:55.10,0:30:56.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's swim it.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:01.19,0:31:04.15,Default,,0,0,0,,- Have a ball, baby.\N- I'm not swimming in that.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:06.20,0:31:09.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, if we could get some rope,\Nwe could make a log bridge!
Dialogue: 0,0:31:12.58,0:31:14.41,Default,,0,0,0,,If we... If we had some logs.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:19.09,0:31:20.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Quark!
Dialogue: 0,0:31:20.21,0:31:21.59,Default,,0,0,0,,- Your dog?\N- Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:21.88,0:31:23.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Quark can't hear us.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:23.21,0:31:25.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, he can. Dogs have great ears.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:25.67,0:31:28.47,Default,,0,0,0,,If we can get on him, he'll take us\Nall the way back to the house.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:28.80,0:31:29.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Whistle.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:43.73,0:31:45.99,Default,,0,0,0,,- What's wrong?\N- He can't whistle.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:49.82,0:31:51.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's get higher up.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:55.12,0:31:56.54,Default,,0,0,0,,You know how to whistle.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:56.79,0:31:59.04,Default,,0,0,0,,You just put your lips together\Nand blow.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:09.01,0:32:11.93,Default,,0,0,0,,From the top of that flower,\Nwe could see over the grass.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:13.97,0:32:15.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's climb!
Dialogue: 0,0:32:21.11,0:32:23.90,Default,,0,0,0,,No, Patty, no, no.\NThere's nothing to worry about.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:24.11,0:32:26.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Just have Amy call me\Nif you hear from her. Thanks.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:28.32,0:32:30.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Amy's not at Patty's, and Nick's not\Nat the Koestlers'.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:30.41,0:32:32.20,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm gonna call Betsy.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:32.41,0:32:34.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, they've got to be somewhere.\NDid you check next door?
Dialogue: 0,0:32:34.91,0:32:37.33,Default,,0,0,0,,At the Thompsons'?\NThey'd rather be in school!
Dialogue: 0,0:32:45.63,0:32:46.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Nick, be careful!
Dialogue: 0,0:32:47.97,0:32:49.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, Mother.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:50.97,0:32:52.18,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll go up with them.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:01.35,0:33:04.19,Default,,0,0,0,,- There was a bee on me.\N- Yeah, right.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:08.44,0:33:09.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait a second.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:11.78,0:33:13.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Nick doesn't play baseball.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:18.83,0:33:20.21,Default,,0,0,0,,I just figured it out.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:20.54,0:33:23.00,Default,,0,0,0,,I never woke up this morning.\NThis is all a bad dream.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:23.46,0:33:26.17,Default,,0,0,0,,- Ron, get up.\N- You're just a nightmare!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:26.42,0:33:28.42,Default,,0,0,0,,When I get up,\NDad and I will be going fishing.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:28.80,0:33:30.17,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm warning you.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:34.14,0:33:37.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay, Ron... maybe you're right.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:38.60,0:33:40.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe this is just all a bad dream.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:41.18,0:33:42.98,Default,,0,0,0,,But if it is...
Dialogue: 0,0:33:44.02,0:33:45.36,Default,,0,0,0,,would this hurt?
Dialogue: 0,0:33:45.44,0:33:46.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Get up!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:48.23,0:33:50.49,Default,,0,0,0,,If you were my brother,\NI'd put myself up for adoption.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:50.57,0:33:53.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah? I hope your face\Nends up on a milk carton.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:04.42,0:34:05.96,Default,,0,0,0,,My chair.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:09.67,0:34:11.05,Default,,0,0,0,,My couch.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:16.39,0:34:17.60,Default,,0,0,0,,It works.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:26.27,0:34:28.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Nick? Amy?
Dialogue: 0,0:34:29.40,0:34:30.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Can you hear me?
Dialogue: 0,0:34:33.03,0:34:34.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Nick.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:33.42,0:35:34.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Uh-huh.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:47.89,0:35:49.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Nick?
Dialogue: 0,0:35:50.44,0:35:51.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Nick!
Dialogue: 0,0:35:56.15,0:35:58.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Nick!
Dialogue: 0,0:35:59.66,0:36:00.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:36:04.33,0:36:07.71,Default,,0,0,0,,When we crashed, my entire life\Nflashed before my eyes.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:09.50,0:36:10.88,Default,,0,0,0,,It didn't take too long.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:15.13,0:36:16.47,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm scared, Russ.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:17.38,0:36:18.97,Default,,0,0,0,,We could be anywhere now.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:21.30,0:36:22.76,Default,,0,0,0,,I think we're still\Nin your yard.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:23.18,0:36:23.97,Default,,0,0,0,,How do you know?
Dialogue: 0,0:36:24.06,0:36:25.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Any other yard,\Nthe grass would be shorter.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:25.97,0:36:28.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, we gotta find\NRon and your sister.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:28.98,0:36:31.65,Default,,0,0,0,,And then if they don't fry him,\Nhe'll go to jail. Your mother, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:31.86,0:36:33.19,Default,,0,0,0,,After all, she's the one\Nwho paid for it.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:33.27,0:36:35.73,Default,,0,0,0,,That makes her an accomplice.\NDo you know what it's like in jail?
Dialogue: 0,0:36:35.82,0:36:37.99,Default,,0,0,0,,I am gonna tell you\None more time to shut up!
Dialogue: 0,0:36:38.07,0:36:41.32,Default,,0,0,0,,And then what? And then you'll smack\Nme? You'll go to jail, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:41.41,0:36:43.49,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll tell them\Nafter a big bee ate my brother,
Dialogue: 0,0:36:43.66,0:36:44.83,Default,,0,0,0,,you smacked me around.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:45.37,0:36:47.54,Default,,0,0,0,,No jury in the world\Nwould fail to convict you.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:48.20,0:36:49.100,Default,,0,0,0,,The whole Szalinski family\Nis gonna be in jail for life!
Dialogue: 0,0:36:50.08,0:36:52.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Look. My dad's machine works.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:52.96,0:36:55.00,Default,,0,0,0,,When we get home\Nand he fixes us all,
Dialogue: 0,0:36:55.09,0:36:57.88,Default,,0,0,0,,we're gonna be so rich,\Nyou'll regret this.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:00.47,0:37:03.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Amy, you know I've\Nalways liked your family.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:03.59,0:37:05.18,Default,,0,0,0,,I mean, your dad's a real nice guy.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:05.51,0:37:07.14,Default,,0,0,0,,He's not as weird\Nas I thought he was.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:07.52,0:37:10.23,Default,,0,0,0,,I love you and Nick\Nlike my own brother and sister.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:30.46,0:37:33.00,Default,,0,0,0,,It's just that my dad\Ndoesn't understand your dad.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:33.12,0:37:35.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Your dad doesn't understand anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:16.96,0:38:20.17,Default,,0,0,0,,No, Cathy. I just thought\Nthey might have stopped by.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:20.26,0:38:22.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay, listen. If you see 'em,\Njust send 'em home?
Dialogue: 0,0:38:23.05,0:38:25.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay. You have a good weekend.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:27.72,0:38:30.27,Default,,0,0,0,,This is getting ridiculous.\NWhere the hell are those kids?
Dialogue: 0,0:38:36.02,0:38:37.44,Default,,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:43.15,0:38:44.07,Default,,0,0,0,,We had to bring the dog.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:44.16,0:38:45.45,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't wanna hear anymore\Nabout the cat.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:45.53,0:38:47.66,Default,,0,0,0,,It's the Forresters.\NWhat are we gonna tell them?
Dialogue: 0,0:38:47.74,0:38:50.74,Default,,0,0,0,,- How about the truth?\N- Mae, what kind of an excuse is that?
Dialogue: 0,0:38:51.75,0:38:52.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Don!
Dialogue: 0,0:38:52.83,0:38:54.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, what's up?
Dialogue: 0,0:38:54.100,0:38:56.92,Default,,0,0,0,,How about catching some...
Dialogue: 0,0:38:59.92,0:39:01.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Good morning, Russell.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:02.05,0:39:04.63,Default,,0,0,0,,- Hi, Gloria.\N- Say good morning, Sushi.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:04.72,0:39:06.14,Default,,0,0,0,,- Don, I...\N- Well, the fishing report
Dialogue: 0,0:39:06.22,0:39:09.18,Default,,0,0,0,,looks stellar. Let's make exhaust\Nwhile the sun still shines, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:39:09.26,0:39:11.26,Default,,0,0,0,,- I called Charlie at Bass Lake.\N- I know, but Don...
Dialogue: 0,0:39:11.35,0:39:12.85,Default,,0,0,0,,He says the fish\Nare jumping on the boat.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:12.93,0:39:14.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh! And I brought my new...
Dialogue: 0,0:39:14.10,0:39:16.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Donald, that man over there\Nis flying.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:17.19,0:39:18.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Right, Gloria.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:18.31,0:39:20.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Don, uh, something's come up.\NI don't think we're gonna be able
Dialogue: 0,0:39:20.86,0:39:22.65,Default,,0,0,0,,to make it.\NMaybe you ought to go on ahead.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:23.07,0:39:24.90,Default,,0,0,0,,What do... What do you mean\Nyou don't think you're gonna
Dialogue: 0,0:39:24.99,0:39:26.61,Default,,0,0,0,,be able to make it?\NWe're caravaning, good buddy!
Dialogue: 0,0:39:26.70,0:39:29.16,Default,,0,0,0,,- Donald, I am...\N- Not now, Gloria!
Dialogue: 0,0:39:29.24,0:39:32.08,Default,,0,0,0,,And besides, if you're not there\Nby six, you'll lose your deposit.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:32.16,0:39:33.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Confidentially...
Dialogue: 0,0:39:35.08,0:39:36.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Mae hasn't been feeling too well.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:38.38,0:39:39.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Plumbing.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:40.75,0:39:41.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Plumbing?
Dialogue: 0,0:39:43.80,0:39:46.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, this isn't the big\NRuss Thompson I know. I mean,
Dialogue: 0,0:39:46.68,0:39:49.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Plumbing would not stop\Nthe big Russ Thompson I know.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:49.59,0:39:51.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Especially with\Nan $80 deposit on the line!
Dialogue: 0,0:39:51.81,0:39:54.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Don, hook a big one for me, okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:40:05.49,0:40:06.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Don?
Dialogue: 0,0:40:11.37,0:40:12.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's roll, Gloria.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:13.24,0:40:14.79,Default,,0,0,0,,- Come on, get in.\N- What's wrong with...
Dialogue: 0,0:40:15.04,0:40:16.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:20.00,0:40:21.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Mm-hmm.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:28.88,0:40:30.76,Default,,0,0,0,,- Did you tell him the truth?\N- Honey!
Dialogue: 0,0:40:32.01,0:40:33.93,Default,,0,0,0,,- Did they take it okay?\N- Mae.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:38.14,0:40:41.44,Default,,0,0,0,,80 bucks, Mae. Non-refundable!
Dialogue: 0,0:40:41.52,0:40:43.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Those kids are grounded!
Dialogue: 0,0:40:51.11,0:40:52.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Ugh...
Dialogue: 0,0:40:52.28,0:40:54.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Mud is still mud,\Nno matter how small you are.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:56.12,0:40:58.71,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't believe some stores\Nactually charge for this stuff.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:03.34,0:41:05.50,Default,,0,0,0,,That was really great,\Nwhat you did for Nick.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:06.63,0:41:09.30,Default,,0,0,0,,What about you, Amy?\NHe saved you, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:12.09,0:41:13.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, I know, Nick.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:16.10,0:41:18.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Where'd you learn\Nartificial respiration?
Dialogue: 0,0:41:21.02,0:41:23.69,Default,,0,0,0,,- French class, kid.\N- Oh.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:25.27,0:41:26.57,Default,,0,0,0,,French class?
Dialogue: 0,0:41:46.25,0:41:47.63,Default,,0,0,0,,How about a truce, okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:41:51.38,0:41:52.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:02.64,0:42:04.86,Default,,0,0,0,,I think this is the flagstone\Nin the middle of the yard.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:05.90,0:42:07.23,Default,,0,0,0,,You mean we're halfway there?
Dialogue: 0,0:42:07.57,0:42:08.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, I think so.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:09.11,0:42:10.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's go!
Dialogue: 0,0:42:17.12,0:42:18.45,Default,,0,0,0,,French class.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:33.22,0:42:35.55,Default,,0,0,0,,I'd die for a strawberry sundae...
Dialogue: 0,0:42:35.97,0:42:38.64,Default,,0,0,0,,with chocolate sprinkles\Nand a banana split.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:40.60,0:42:43.02,Default,,0,0,0,,I could eat a corn dog\Nthe size of a truck.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:44.14,0:42:47.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Ron, if you had a corn dog,\Nit would be the size of a truck.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:49.44,0:42:51.15,Default,,0,0,0,,I've died and gone to heaven.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:51.44,0:42:53.07,Default,,0,0,0,,It's as big as a house!
Dialogue: 0,0:42:53.49,0:42:54.82,Default,,0,0,0,,I saw it first! It's mine!
Dialogue: 0,0:42:55.99,0:42:58.12,Default,,0,0,0,,I got dibs on the cream filling!
Dialogue: 0,0:42:58.28,0:42:59.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Nick, it's one of your cookies!
Dialogue: 0,0:43:09.88,0:43:11.80,Default,,0,0,0,,They're never gonna\Nbelieve this at school.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:12.67,0:43:13.88,Default,,0,0,0,,You guys, come on.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:14.72,0:43:16.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Somebody take this cookie!
Dialogue: 0,0:43:17.51,0:43:19.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Nicky, take this thing!
Dialogue: 0,0:43:20.51,0:43:22.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Help! Nicky!
Dialogue: 0,0:43:24.48,0:43:26.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, you guys.\NThis is your ant!
Dialogue: 0,0:43:27.65,0:43:29.27,Default,,0,0,0,,- Nicky, help me!\N- She did it.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:30.23,0:43:31.69,Default,,0,0,0,,- Somebody help me!\N- You know...
Dialogue: 0,0:43:32.53,0:43:34.61,Default,,0,0,0,,- your sister's not bad...\N- Nicky!
Dialogue: 0,0:43:34.82,0:43:36.66,Default,,0,0,0,,- for a girl.\N- Of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:50.50,0:43:53.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you, officer. We'd appreciate\Nyou sending somebody by.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:53.51,0:43:55.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, okay, it's 646--
Dialogue: 0,0:43:59.97,0:44:02.31,Default,,0,0,0,,That guy's got serious problems.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:03.26,0:44:05.10,Default,,0,0,0,,<i>Mrs. Thompson. Hello?</i>
Dialogue: 0,0:44:06.02,0:44:08.94,Default,,0,0,0,,646 Sycamore. Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:12.44,0:44:14.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Great idea, Russ,
Dialogue: 0,0:44:14.19,0:44:16.11,Default,,0,0,0,,even if the boy genius\Ndidn't think of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:16.20,0:44:17.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Drawbridge!
Dialogue: 0,0:44:21.28,0:44:23.03,Default,,0,0,0,,At this rate,\Nwe'll be home by dinner.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:24.20,0:44:25.100,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe I can still go out...
Dialogue: 0,0:44:27.58,0:44:28.83,Default,,0,0,0,,with Patty.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:29.92,0:44:33.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, our weekend's shot.\NWe'll never get to go camping now.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:33.55,0:44:35.84,Default,,0,0,0,,I know Dad.\NWe're grounded.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:36.26,0:44:38.22,Default,,0,0,0,,We are camping, Ron. Only better.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:38.88,0:44:40.18,Default,,0,0,0,,This is like a safari.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:40.47,0:44:43.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, yeah. I never thought\Nof it that way, you know?
Dialogue: 0,0:44:44.18,0:44:45.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Onward!
Dialogue: 0,0:45:02.70,0:45:04.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Amy?
Dialogue: 0,0:45:05.12,0:45:06.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Nick?
Dialogue: 0,0:45:07.100,0:45:09.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Wayne?
Dialogue: 0,0:45:18.42,0:45:22.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah. Um, I would like to report,\Num, two missing children.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:22.14,0:45:24.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, instead of flapping\Nyour gums about it, why don't you go out--
Dialogue: 0,0:45:24.68,0:45:26.10,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm sure\Nit's nothing to worry about.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:26.18,0:45:28.81,Default,,0,0,0,,This sort of thing happens all the time.\NYou have a little spat
Dialogue: 0,0:45:28.89,0:45:30.39,Default,,0,0,0,,- with the kids...\N- Whoa, we did not have a spat.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:30.52,0:45:32.48,Default,,0,0,0,,You were kind of upset\Nabout Russ quitting the team, hon.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:32.56,0:45:34.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Quit! I thought he was cut!
Dialogue: 0,0:45:34.61,0:45:36.44,Default,,0,0,0,,He was afraid to tell you he quit.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:36.53,0:45:38.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Quit... What do you mean\Nhe was afraid to tell me?
Dialogue: 0,0:45:38.69,0:45:40.74,Default,,0,0,0,,He can tell me anything he wants.\NYou know me! I always listen!
Dialogue: 0,0:45:40.86,0:45:42.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Uh-huh.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:42.99,0:45:44.32,Default,,0,0,0,,What's "uh-huh" supposed\Nto mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:45:44.41,0:45:45.95,Default,,0,0,0,,- Russell!\N- No. I don't like the way he said it.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:46.03,0:45:47.99,Default,,0,0,0,,You don't need\Nto get upset, Mr. Thomson.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:48.29,0:45:50.04,Default,,0,0,0,,You know, it's not unusual\Nfor these runaways...
Dialogue: 0,0:45:50.12,0:45:53.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Whoa, my kids\Ndid not run away. They're happy kids,
Dialogue: 0,0:45:53.17,0:45:55.34,Default,,0,0,0,,and there's no way you can make\Nme believe that they ran away!
Dialogue: 0,0:45:56.50,0:45:57.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Here he goes with his writing again.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:57.76,0:45:59.97,Default,,0,0,0,,- Don't you ever say ever anything?\N- Uh-huh.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:00.05,0:46:01.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Russell!
Dialogue: 0,0:46:02.30,0:46:04.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Why do I feel like\NI am the one on trial here?
Dialogue: 0,0:46:05.01,0:46:07.60,Default,,0,0,0,,- I can't imagine, dear.\N- What do you mean, you can't imagine?
Dialogue: 0,0:46:07.68,0:46:10.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, I think we have enough\Nto get started.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:10.27,0:46:13.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Please, give us a call\Nif you hear from the boys.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:13.35,0:46:14.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:22.82,0:46:24.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't they need\Na warrant or something?
Dialogue: 0,0:46:24.82,0:46:27.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Russell, there's a few\Nthings about yourself
Dialogue: 0,0:46:27.45,0:46:28.74,Default,,0,0,0,,I think you should know.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:29.58,0:46:31.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, like what?
Dialogue: 0,0:46:31.83,0:46:33.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, I think you need\Nto sit down...
Dialogue: 0,0:46:36.13,0:46:38.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, another\Nmissing children report.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:39.09,0:46:40.84,Default,,0,0,0,,644 Sycamore.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:42.13,0:46:43.43,Default,,0,0,0,,That's next door.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:44.97,0:46:47.10,Default,,0,0,0,,I called the police.\NWhat's on your head?
Dialogue: 0,0:46:47.30,0:46:49.64,Default,,0,0,0,,- I was looking for the kids.\N- Where, in a coal mine?
Dialogue: 0,0:46:49.72,0:46:51.89,Default,,0,0,0,,- They're in the backyard.\N- They are?
Dialogue: 0,0:46:51.98,0:46:54.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Diane, I got something\Nreal important to tell you.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:55.02,0:46:56.90,Default,,0,0,0,,That is the couch from the attic.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:58.82,0:47:00.57,Default,,0,0,0,,You can see the marks\Nwhere Quark chewed the arms.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:00.65,0:47:02.99,Default,,0,0,0,,I found it on the floor.\NIt's my thinking couch.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:04.28,0:47:05.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Wayne...
Dialogue: 0,0:47:06.66,0:47:07.99,Default,,0,0,0,,are you trying to tell me...
Dialogue: 0,0:47:09.66,0:47:10.74,Default,,0,0,0,,you did it?
Dialogue: 0,0:47:11.62,0:47:12.75,Default,,0,0,0,,It works?
Dialogue: 0,0:47:13.29,0:47:14.62,Default,,0,0,0,,The machine works?
Dialogue: 0,0:47:15.25,0:47:17.92,Default,,0,0,0,,- Do the kids know?\N- Well, yeah. The kids know.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:18.25,0:47:20.09,Default,,0,0,0,,- That's great.\N- It's not that great.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:20.25,0:47:21.84,Default,,0,0,0,,- Why?\N- I shrunk the kids.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:22.72,0:47:24.13,Default,,0,0,0,,- What?\N- And the Thompson kids, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:24.22,0:47:25.84,Default,,0,0,0,,They're about this big.\NThey're in the backyard.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:26.14,0:47:28.05,Default,,0,0,0,,- What?\N- I threw them out with the trash.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:28.26,0:47:30.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Stay here. I'll get the door.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:32.68,0:47:33.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes?
Dialogue: 0,0:47:34.64,0:47:37.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Did, uh, you report\Nsome missing children?
Dialogue: 0,0:47:38.65,0:47:40.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, there must be some mistake.\NOurs are in the backyard.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:41.23,0:47:42.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Right, honey?
Dialogue: 0,0:47:45.70,0:47:46.91,Default,,0,0,0,,She's...
Dialogue: 0,0:47:47.86,0:47:49.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you!
Dialogue: 0,0:48:03.76,0:48:06.80,Default,,0,0,0,,How are you doing, boy?\NHow about a pit stop?
Dialogue: 0,0:48:13.14,0:48:15.73,Default,,0,0,0,,- What is it, Ron?\N- Antie needs a recharge.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:22.61,0:48:23.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Here, you deserve this.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:25.99,0:48:28.07,Default,,0,0,0,,We're not gonna make it before dark.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:29.11,0:48:30.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, even if we did,
Dialogue: 0,0:48:30.99,0:48:32.37,Default,,0,0,0,,the mall would be closed.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:33.03,0:48:34.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't eat so fast.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:34.95,0:48:36.100,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey... that's my hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:40.12,0:48:41.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Why don't we let him go?
Dialogue: 0,0:48:41.63,0:48:43.75,Default,,0,0,0,,He's worn out, and his family\Nmight be worried about him.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:44.67,0:48:47.59,Default,,0,0,0,,- It's okay with me.\N- Yeah, me too, I guess.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:47.76,0:48:49.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Help me get off the harness.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:59.27,0:49:00.52,Default,,0,0,0,,You can go now.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:05.32,0:49:07.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on. Just start walking.\NHe'll get the idea.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:10.95,0:49:12.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Thanks for the lift, Antie.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:13.28,0:49:15.49,Default,,0,0,0,,You're free.\NYou get home now.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:16.12,0:49:18.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Shoo!
Dialogue: 0,0:49:20.62,0:49:22.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Looks like you've got a new pet.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:22.58,0:49:24.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Dumb ant doesn't know\Nwhat's best for him.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:26.38,0:49:28.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Go on! Go home!
Dialogue: 0,0:49:28.55,0:49:30.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Mom will never let me keep you.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:37.56,0:49:38.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Amy?
Dialogue: 0,0:49:39.06,0:49:40.27,Default,,0,0,0,,- Nick?\N- Nick?
Dialogue: 0,0:49:40.48,0:49:42.44,Default,,0,0,0,,- Are you there, kids?\N- Nicky!
Dialogue: 0,0:49:43.44,0:49:44.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Where are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:49:47.15,0:49:49.11,Default,,0,0,0,,- Any luck?\N- No.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:05.71,0:50:06.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Nick?
Dialogue: 0,0:50:08.42,0:50:09.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Amy?
Dialogue: 0,0:50:13.68,0:50:15.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you see anything yet?
Dialogue: 0,0:50:15.93,0:50:17.31,Default,,0,0,0,,It's too thick.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:18.39,0:50:20.06,Default,,0,0,0,,It's supposed to be thick.\NIt's grass!
Dialogue: 0,0:50:21.89,0:50:22.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Keep looking.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:23.39,0:50:25.23,Default,,0,0,0,,- Nick?\N- Amy?
Dialogue: 0,0:50:31.74,0:50:33.91,Default,,0,0,0,,- What was that?\N- Ow!
Dialogue: 0,0:50:34.45,0:50:36.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Wa... Watch out!
Dialogue: 0,0:50:38.49,0:50:39.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:49.17,0:50:51.42,Default,,0,0,0,,- Ugh...\N- Where did that come from?
Dialogue: 0,0:50:58.68,0:51:01.22,Default,,0,0,0,,- Yeah, it's Dad's brand.\N- He told us he quit!
Dialogue: 0,0:51:05.02,0:51:07.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Ugh. Looks like he started up again.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:08.32,0:51:10.98,Default,,0,0,0,,No, he only smokes when\Nhe's really worried about something.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:13.28,0:51:16.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Nicky, be careful!
Dialogue: 0,0:51:18.57,0:51:20.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey. Hey, maybe we can use this.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:36.93,0:51:39.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Cool! Now, we can see in the dark!
Dialogue: 0,0:51:45.60,0:51:48.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, Antie, look! Headlights!
Dialogue: 0,0:51:49.48,0:51:51.02,Default,,0,0,0,,I didn't force him\Nto join the team.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:51.11,0:51:54.49,Default,,0,0,0,,I know, but you always\Nmake such a big deal out of sports!
Dialogue: 0,0:51:54.65,0:51:55.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Because sports build character.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:55.86,0:51:57.61,Default,,0,0,0,,No, they don't.\NThey build muscle!
Dialogue: 0,0:51:58.53,0:52:00.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Russell, you've got to understand...
Dialogue: 0,0:52:01.12,0:52:02.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Wayne?
Dialogue: 0,0:52:02.12,0:52:04.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah?
Dialogue: 0,0:52:04.100,0:52:06.58,Default,,0,0,0,,We've got to tell the Thompsons.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:17.76,0:52:20.01,Default,,0,0,0,,What do you take me for?\NA complete idiot?
Dialogue: 0,0:52:21.18,0:52:23.18,Default,,0,0,0,,- How did this happen?\N- Hold on a second, Mae.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:23.51,0:52:24.68,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll handle it, all right?
Dialogue: 0,0:52:25.73,0:52:26.68,Default,,0,0,0,,How did this happen?
Dialogue: 0,0:52:26.77,0:52:28.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, the machine analyzes\Nthe molecular structure
Dialogue: 0,0:52:28.69,0:52:31.15,Default,,0,0,0,,of each compound, and then\Nthrough laser inversion, it takes...
Dialogue: 0,0:52:31.23,0:52:34.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait, Wayne, wait. I think\Nthe Thompsons need to see the couch.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:36.70,0:52:38.86,Default,,0,0,0,,This guy is a waste of skin.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:40.82,0:52:42.87,Default,,0,0,0,,- This is a microscope.\N- I know.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:44.79,0:52:45.100,Default,,0,0,0,,Look in there.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:47.25,0:52:48.37,Default,,0,0,0,,All right.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:49.71,0:52:52.17,Default,,0,0,0,,You see, that's the couch that used\Nto be sitting right over here
Dialogue: 0,0:52:52.25,0:52:53.46,Default,,0,0,0,,until the machine shrunk it.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:53.55,0:52:55.17,Default,,0,0,0,,All right,\Nso there's some doll furniture.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:55.30,0:52:57.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Big deal. They sell\Nthat kind of stuff at swap meets!
Dialogue: 0,0:52:58.88,0:53:00.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Why didn't you tell us earlier?
Dialogue: 0,0:53:00.93,0:53:03.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, until now,\Nthe machine just blew things up.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:04.10,0:53:05.97,Default,,0,0,0,,- Are you saying that machine blew...\N- Blew up my kids?
Dialogue: 0,0:53:06.06,0:53:07.43,Default,,0,0,0,,- No, no, no.\N- No, no, no.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:07.52,0:53:10.27,Default,,0,0,0,,If the machine had blown up the kids,\Nthere'd be pieces of them everywhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:10.35,0:53:11.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Wayne!
Dialogue: 0,0:53:12.31,0:53:13.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Sorry, I...
Dialogue: 0,0:53:13.77,0:53:16.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Look, I'm positive about this, okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:53:16.69,0:53:18.03,Default,,0,0,0,,The machine shrunk our kids.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:18.20,0:53:19.70,Default,,0,0,0,,You're the one who needs\Na shrink, Szalinski!
Dialogue: 0,0:53:19.78,0:53:21.70,Default,,0,0,0,,- Russell!\N- You are a nutcase.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:21.78,0:53:25.53,Default,,0,0,0,,And I'll tell you something.\NI have got an air hammer in my attic.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:25.70,0:53:27.24,Default,,0,0,0,,And if you did do something\Nto my kids,
Dialogue: 0,0:53:27.33,0:53:29.16,Default,,0,0,0,,there's gonna be pieces of you\Nall over the neighborhood!
Dialogue: 0,0:53:29.33,0:53:30.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, honey.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:36.84,0:53:39.34,Default,,0,0,0,,I think that went well.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:40.30,0:53:42.14,Default,,0,0,0,,I think we should have them\Nover more often.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:43.01,0:53:44.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, well,\Nit's a priority for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:45.47,0:53:47.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Now why don't you do\Nwhat you're paid to do?
Dialogue: 0,0:53:49.14,0:53:50.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Find my kids.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:03.28,0:54:04.57,Default,,0,0,0,,I thought you didn't believe him.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:06.41,0:54:07.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, I don't.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:09.58,0:54:10.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Electricity's cheap.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:35.44,0:54:36.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on!
Dialogue: 0,0:54:37.02,0:54:39.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Look at this!\NWe don't have to sleep on the ground.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:43.61,0:54:45.78,Default,,0,0,0,,- What is it?\N- One of my legos.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:46.91,0:54:48.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Give me a boost!
Dialogue: 0,0:54:52.75,0:54:54.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey...
Dialogue: 0,0:54:55.54,0:54:56.71,Default,,0,0,0,,not bad.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:58.96,0:54:59.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:00.05,0:55:01.84,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't even have to brush my teeth!
Dialogue: 0,0:55:03.55,0:55:04.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Quit pushing!
Dialogue: 0,0:55:04.89,0:55:07.26,Default,,0,0,0,,- Move over!\N- You move over!
Dialogue: 0,0:55:08.39,0:55:10.60,Default,,0,0,0,,- Why don't you take that one?\N- Are you sure?
Dialogue: 0,0:55:11.56,0:55:13.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah. I'd rather sleep down here.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:20.69,0:55:21.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Night, Antie.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:26.49,0:55:27.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Think they'll be warm enough?
Dialogue: 0,0:55:28.70,0:55:30.16,Default,,0,0,0,,They look fine to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:42.88,0:55:43.92,Default,,0,0,0,,You think you'll be warm enough?
Dialogue: 0,0:55:43.92,0:55:44.42,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:46.18,0:55:47.76,Default,,0,0,0,,That's not what I meant.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:49.22,0:55:51.85,Default,,0,0,0,,You know,\Nit's not important...
Dialogue: 0,0:55:52.72,0:55:54.35,Default,,0,0,0,,if I sell another house,
Dialogue: 0,0:55:55.48,0:55:57.94,Default,,0,0,0,,or if you get a grant\Nthis year or next.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:00.15,0:56:02.53,Default,,0,0,0,,We've just got to get\Nthis family back together.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:05.99,0:56:07.61,Default,,0,0,0,,I feel the same way.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:17.54,0:56:20.13,Default,,0,0,0,,I gotta fix the machine.\NYou should get some sleep.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:20.79,0:56:23.13,Default,,0,0,0,,We gotta get up early and come\Nout here and look for them.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:24.59,0:56:25.97,Default,,0,0,0,,No, I couldn't sleep.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:27.80,0:56:29.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Not with my babies\Nout here all alone.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:30.93,0:56:33.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah, don't worry about them. They got\Nthe Thompson kids with them.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:33.93,0:56:35.14,Default,,0,0,0,,They'll be fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:36.93,0:56:38.77,Default,,0,0,0,,That's another thing\NI'm worried about.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:39.69,0:56:41.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Amy in the dark...
Dialogue: 0,0:56:42.57,0:56:44.03,Default,,0,0,0,,with little Russ Thompson.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:44.57,0:56:45.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Get some rest.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:52.41,0:56:54.29,Default,,0,0,0,,They'd better behave themselves.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:59.33,0:57:00.67,Default,,0,0,0,,It's funny.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:01.54,0:57:04.13,Default,,0,0,0,,The moon looks the same size\Nwhether you're big or small.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:04.59,0:57:07.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah. Tell that to my dad.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:09.18,0:57:11.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Why? Does he pick on you\Nabout your size?
Dialogue: 0,0:57:12.68,0:57:14.43,Default,,0,0,0,,The bigger the guy,\Nthe bigger the moon.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:16.02,0:57:17.52,Default,,0,0,0,,It's just the way he thinks.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:18.68,0:57:19.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Russ?
Dialogue: 0,0:57:21.40,0:57:23.65,Default,,0,0,0,,- Yeah?\N- How come you never came over before?
Dialogue: 0,0:57:25.90,0:57:26.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Well...
Dialogue: 0,0:57:31.07,0:57:32.16,Default,,0,0,0,,I mean...
Dialogue: 0,0:57:32.87,0:57:35.03,Default,,0,0,0,,you talked to me\Nonce or twice last year.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:36.41,0:57:39.33,Default,,0,0,0,,I mean, I would've come by.\NI wanted to, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:57:41.83,0:57:43.84,Default,,0,0,0,,I guess I always thought\Nyou were too popular to notice me.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:45.50,0:57:47.38,Default,,0,0,0,,I was too popular to notice.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:49.42,0:57:50.63,Default,,0,0,0,,I was stupid.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:19.08,0:58:21.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Nicky!
Dialogue: 0,0:58:23.12,0:58:23.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Look, it's the rest of them.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:26.29,0:58:27.92,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm gonna go get the Thompsons.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:28.17,0:58:29.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Hang on, kids!
Dialogue: 0,0:58:31.47,0:58:33.89,Default,,0,0,0,,It obviously worked on the kids.\NI just don't get it.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:35.68,0:58:37.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, you better get it, Szalinski.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:37.51,0:58:39.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Russ, you're not helping.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:39.47,0:58:42.10,Default,,0,0,0,,- So, I'm not helping.\N- Russell, you got to understand.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:43.19,0:58:44.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Baseball!
Dialogue: 0,0:58:44.77,0:58:46.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Nick's trying to say something.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:47.19,0:58:48.69,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't make it out.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:51.45,0:58:53.53,Default,,0,0,0,,The baseball, Dad!
Dialogue: 0,0:58:54.20,0:58:55.99,Default,,0,0,0,,What are you saying, Nick?
Dialogue: 0,0:59:00.29,0:59:01.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Swinging?
Dialogue: 0,0:59:01.91,0:59:04.62,Default,,0,0,0,,- Sounds like--\N- It's semaphore, Mae.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:04.71,0:59:07.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait! Uh...uh, flapping!
Dialogue: 0,0:59:07.59,0:59:08.88,Default,,0,0,0,,- Pitching.\N- Um...
Dialogue: 0,0:59:09.13,0:59:11.09,Default,,0,0,0,,- Throwing.\N- You're out! You're out!
Dialogue: 0,0:59:11.63,0:59:12.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Baseball!
Dialogue: 0,0:59:13.05,0:59:14.13,Default,,0,0,0,,- Yes!\N- Right!
Dialogue: 0,0:59:14.26,0:59:15.80,Default,,0,0,0,,- The baseball!\N- The ball!
Dialogue: 0,0:59:16.05,0:59:17.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Baseball?
Dialogue: 0,0:59:17.85,0:59:19.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Good, honey.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:22.10,0:59:24.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Holy smokes. It's the laser!
Dialogue: 0,0:59:26.44,0:59:28.57,Default,,0,0,0,,I got it.\NThe ball came through the window,
Dialogue: 0,0:59:28.94,0:59:30.36,Default,,0,0,0,,and activated the machine,
Dialogue: 0,0:59:31.19,0:59:32.86,Default,,0,0,0,,and got in the path of the laser.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:33.49,0:59:34.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Why didn't I think of this before?
Dialogue: 0,0:59:35.36,0:59:37.20,Default,,0,0,0,,- I could take a wild guess.\N- Shh!
Dialogue: 0,0:59:37.28,0:59:39.41,Default,,0,0,0,,It's creating too much heat\NThat's way everything was blowing up!
Dialogue: 0,0:59:39.70,0:59:42.20,Default,,0,0,0,,- Thanks, Nick!\N- All right, Nicky!
Dialogue: 0,0:59:42.29,0:59:43.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Diane, you take the spoon.\NI'll get the machine...
Dialogue: 0,0:59:43.75,0:59:46.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Hold it, Szalinski.\NThis gizmo's been blowing up fruit.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:46.37,0:59:48.88,Default,,0,0,0,,And you're not trying it on my kids\Nuntil you try is on something living!
Dialogue: 0,0:59:53.17,0:59:55.01,Default,,0,0,0,,You know something?\NMaybe I should do it on myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:55.09,0:59:56.89,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll show you how to\Nwork the machine. It's not that hard.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:56.97,0:59:58.89,Default,,0,0,0,,No, no!
Dialogue: 0,0:59:59.09,1:00:02.06,Default,,0,0,0,,- Do it on me.\N- Are you sure, honey?
Dialogue: 0,1:00:07.52,1:00:08.94,Default,,0,0,0,,How'd those get there?
Dialogue: 0,1:00:24.87,1:00:26.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay, Szalinski,
Dialogue: 0,1:00:26.83,1:00:27.75,Default,,0,0,0,,shoot.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:28.54,1:00:30.38,Default,,0,0,0,,- No reason this shouldn't work now.\N- Huh?
Dialogue: 0,1:00:45.47,1:00:46.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Stand back!
Dialogue: 0,1:00:46.89,1:00:50.98,Default,,0,0,0,,- Honey, you're so brave.\N- Come on, Mae. Come on. Come.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:04.74,1:01:07.75,Default,,0,0,0,,- Russ, are you okay?\N- Yeah, why?
Dialogue: 0,1:01:23.68,1:01:24.81,Default,,0,0,0,,So...
Dialogue: 0,1:01:25.72,1:01:26.97,Default,,0,0,0,,if this works,
Dialogue: 0,1:01:27.06,1:01:28.64,Default,,0,0,0,,do you want to go\Nto the dance on Friday?
Dialogue: 0,1:01:30.06,1:01:31.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Can you dance?
Dialogue: 0,1:01:33.69,1:01:36.40,Default,,0,0,0,,- Not really.\N- I'd love to.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:56.50,1:01:57.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh!
Dialogue: 0,1:01:57.42,1:01:58.97,Default,,0,0,0,,- Russ, Ron!\N- Dad!
Dialogue: 0,1:01:59.05,1:02:02.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, I knew my boys wouldn't run away.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:03.64,1:02:05.97,Default,,0,0,0,,- Are you and Dad okay?\N- Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:06.06,1:02:06.39,Default,,0,0,0,,- All the way across the yard....\N- We're great.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:06.51,1:02:09.64,Default,,0,0,0,,I wanted to go fishing, Dad.\NI didn't mean to mess everything up.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:09.73,1:02:11.94,Default,,0,0,0,,- I know, Ronnie. I know.\N- Dad?
Dialogue: 0,1:02:12.73,1:02:14.11,Default,,0,0,0,,If you really want me\Nback on the team...
Dialogue: 0,1:02:14.19,1:02:16.44,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't care about the team.\NI care about you!
Dialogue: 0,1:02:17.15,1:02:18.65,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm proud of you.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:20.40,1:02:21.53,Default,,0,0,0,,I need to take a shower!
Dialogue: 0,1:02:21.70,1:02:22.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Szalinski.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:32.46,1:02:33.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's eat!
Dialogue: 0,1:02:33.71,1:02:35.17,Default,,0,0,0,,- Honey, make a toast.\N- Good idea.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:35.25,1:02:36.54,Default,,0,0,0,,- Oh, great.\N- Oh, I love toasts.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:36.63,1:02:38.51,Default,,0,0,0,,To the Thompsons and the Szalinskis,
Dialogue: 0,1:02:38.59,1:02:40.09,Default,,0,0,0,,- and many more dinners together.\N- Cheers.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:40.17,1:02:41.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Though I think
Dialogue: 0,1:02:41.30,1:02:42.93,Default,,0,0,0,,we're gonna be having leftovers\Nfor a while.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:43.55,1:02:45.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Wonder what's for dinner.\NRight, Russ?
Dialogue: 0,1:02:45.84,1:02:47.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, I guess I gotta carve\Nthis thing, huh?
Dialogue: 0,1:02:47.35,1:02:49.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, want to use\Nmy chainsaw?
Dialogue: 0,1:02:49.10,1:02:50.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Who wants bread?
Dialogue: 0,1:03:02.45,1:03:03.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, wait!
Dialogue: 0,1:03:04.32,1:03:05.61,Default,,0,0,0,,I get it!
Dialogue: 0,1:03:06.41,1:03:09.20,Default,,0,0,0,,French class! Ha-ha!